{"name":"Cherry Red","hex":"#f7022a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cherry red","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep bright red color, like that of a cherry."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep bright red colour, like that of a cherry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry_red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherry Red Records","blocks":[{"text":"Cherry Red Records is a British independent record label founded in Malvern, Worcestershire, by Iain McNay in 1978. The label has released recordings by Dead Kennedys, Everything but the Girl, The Monochrome Set, and Felt, among others, as well as the compilation album Pillows & Prayers. In addition to releasing new music, Cherry Red also acts as an umbrella for individual imprints and catalogue specialists."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Red_Records"},{"title":"Cherry Red (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cherry Red is an album by the American saxophonist/vocalist Eddie \"Cleanhead\" Vinson recorded in New York in 1967 and released by the BluesWay label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/40/Cherry_Red_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Red_(album)"},{"title":"Cherry Red (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cherry Red\" is a song by the Bee Gees, written by Barry Gibb, released as the B-side of \"I Want Home\" in March 1966, and has become one of the famous Bee Gees songs in the Philippines and Brazil. The song's opening chord was E followed by Barry singing Where are you?."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cf/Cherry_Red.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Red_(song)"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org